{"nodes": [{"id": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "label": "SYSTEM.md: how GLUE works now", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One place that says how GLUE works today. ADRs say why. Updated in the same commit as any change to how GLUE works."}, {"id": "vault_system_pieces", "label": "Four pieces: website, GLUE folder, GLUE Home, GLUE Cloud", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The website works alone, offline and without an account. GLUE Home is the library's engine while it runs, and the website on that computer is its screen."}, {"id": "vault_system_glue_folder", "label": "GLUE folder: JSON files, no database", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The user's data is JSON files in the GLUE folder, no database. Lowercase mco names are real file and setting names, kept because data depends on them."}, {"id": "vault_system_computer_uses", "label": "How a computer uses GLUE: just this computer, synced, with GLUE Home, another device", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A device that only signs in browses. Its songs come from the computers that hold them, streamed."}, {"id": "vault_system_profiles", "label": "Profiles: the account's artist aliases, one library per GLUE folder", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A profile is an artist alias. The account keeps the union of every device's profiles; each device keeps its own choice."}, {"id": "vault_system_shared_collections", "label": "Shared collections: the account's, the same on every device", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With cloud sync on, every collection is the account's and has one copy in GLUE Cloud. The same file on two computers is one song with a copy on each. Only the GLUE folder recorded for a computer writes that computer's parts."}, {"id": "vault_system_shared_sync", "label": "Shared sync: snapshot and log in GLUE Cloud, merged per field", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GLUE Cloud keeps a snapshot and a log of changes; only changed files are looked at, plus every file every 30 minutes. Clashes wait in a box for the user. A computer never clashes with itself."}, {"id": "vault_system_glue_home_engine", "label": "GLUE Home is Rust: its engine, service, stores and analysis queue", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Since 0.52 to 0.60 the engine does the library's work in Rust, and its window shows the status. The page is only the screen when GLUE Home runs."}, {"id": "vault_system_dj_apps_sync", "label": "DJ apps synced both ways through GLUE Home (Engine DJ first)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Opt-in per library, a backup first, and the app closed before any write. Engine DJ's cues, loops and grids merge three ways per slot. Its playlists stay in its DJ collection; GLUE's own go to its GLUE folder."}, {"id": "vault_system_glue_home_cache", "label": "GLUE Home's caches, tidied daily", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Files of songs no longer in their collection are removed after a two-day grace. Overviews and details come from GLUE Home's cache when the browser has none, so a song page never re-analyses in Home mode."}, {"id": "vault_system_local_link", "label": "Local link to GLUE Home on 127.0.0.1 ports 47400 to 47409", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every route except hello and connect needs the token. Any browser on the computer takes its link from GLUE Home. Stopped, it answers only GLUE Home's own windows."}, {"id": "vault_system_streaming_sessions", "label": "Streaming songs to other devices over WebRTC through sessions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each device's tab keeps one session with each of the account's other GLUE Homes, at most five. Songs stream as they arrive through the service worker. Connections are bounded, and a silent room is reconnected."}, {"id": "vault_system_load_priority", "label": "What the user asks for goes first: gated and paced background loads", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "While a song plays, GLUE Home starts no new analysis beyond two. Rows on screen get what they asked for, and a list keeps its place while it changes by itself."}, {"id": "vault_system_covers_no_audio_js", "label": "Covers, waveforms and incoming songs handled by the Rust engine, no audio JavaScript", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Covers from the tags and from public services, with the user's Discogs token sent to Discogs only. A homeBundle test fails if the GLUE Home bundle reaches the website's analysis code."}, {"id": "vault_system_analysis", "label": "Analysis: native in GLUE Home, worker pool in the browser", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The native engine is a line-for-line port held to the TypeScript results. FLAC is decoded by GLUE itself. DSD is analysed as its PCM conversion. Failures that pass are retried, never stored."}, {"id": "vault_system_verdicts", "label": "Quality verdicts: hi-res judged above 24 kHz, lowpass as lossless", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A hi-res file is judged by what reaches past 24 kHz above digital silence. A steep top end that follows the music is a mastering lowpass, shown as lossless. Stored verdicts are judged again from kept details when the rules change."}, {"id": "vault_system_duplicates", "label": "Duplicates: fingerprints and names, the best copy only", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only copies of the same version count. The user can mark copies apart or as duplicates. Only the best copy is shown and used, and GLUE Home makes the groups where it runs."}, {"id": "vault_system_discogs", "label": "Discogs collection, records and playlists", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GLUE Home reads the Discogs collection and wantlist into the profile and matches them to songs. Discogs playlists mix songs and vinyl tracks, kept under Discogs."}, {"id": "vault_system_glue_cloud_accounts", "label": "GLUE Cloud: accounts, devices, collections, signaling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accounts by Google or email and password. A browser that only looks is a browse session. GLUE Cloud holds collections, profiles and devices, never music."}, {"id": "vault_system_gluey_tours", "label": "Gluey: tours as data, help articles, seen across account and GLUE folder", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The first tour shows once per person; seen is the union of the browser's, the GLUE folder's and the account's. A feature's change updates its help article and its tour."}, {"id": "vault_system_look", "label": "Look: the theme table, Hallmark's Console treatment, icons and parts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The theme table generates every theme's tokens; no literal colour in a component. Labels are sentence case, mono only for what was measured, Icon.svelte instead of emoji, Parts.svelte instead of middle dots."}, {"id": "vault_system_next", "label": "Next: events naming a profile; the rekordbox XML export with cues and grid", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_pieces", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_glue_folder", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_computer_uses", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_profiles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_shared_collections", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_shared_sync", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_glue_home_engine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_dj_apps_sync", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_glue_home_cache", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_local_link", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_streaming_sessions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_load_priority", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_covers_no_audio_js", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_analysis", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_verdicts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_duplicates", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_discogs", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "target": "vault_system_glue_cloud_accounts", "relation": "references", 